 "section_summary": "This section contains records concerning post-war educational reform and oversight in occupied Japan. It features the concluding portion and cover sheets of an English translation of the Japanese Ministry of Education textbook 'Democracy', which contrasts democratic principles with Marxist-Leninist communism. A major part consists of SCAP and diplomatic communications addressing illegal operations, communist infiltration, and enforcement measures concerning Korean-operated schools in Yamaguchi Prefecture. The section also includes intelligence reports on the wartime Heishikan Institute established for Nisei, diplomatic inquiries regarding British teachers, and an appraisal of broader educational reforms.",
 "subfiles": [
  {
   "about": "English translation of a chapter from the Japanese Ministry of Education textbook contrasting democracy with communism.",
   "continues_previous": true,
   "date": "1948-10-30",
   "doc_type": "textbook",
